Q12) How have you integrated security into your JobNest project?

“In my JobNest project, security is important to protect user data and restrict unauthorized access.
I focus on the following security measures:

1. Authentication: Verify user credentials before allowing access to protected features.
2. Authorization: Restrict admin operations, such as managing job listings, to users with the appropriate role.
3. Password Security: Store passwords as secure hashes instead of plain text.
4. API Security: Protect restricted REST APIs so unauthorized users cannot access them.
5. Input Validation: Validate user inputs to prevent invalid data from entering the application.
6. Configuration Security: Keep database credentials and secret keys outside the source code.
These measures help improve the security of the application. I would also test authentication, authorization, and invalid requests to verify that the security rules work correctly.”


