Q13) How does OOP work in your JobNest project?

“In my JobNest project, I use Object-Oriented Programming concepts to organize the backend code and make it reusable and maintainable.

Encapsulation: I use classes such as Job to group job-related data and methods. Fields can be kept private and accessed through getters, setters, or controlled methods.

Abstraction: I separate business logic from database operations using layers such as service classes and repository interfaces.

Inheritance: In Spring Data JPA, my repository interface can extend JpaRepository, which provides common database operations without requiring me to implement them manually.

Polymorphism: Spring Data JPA provides repository interfaces whose methods are implemented by the framework at runtime. This lets me use common repository methods through an interface.
These OOP concepts help make the JobNest backend modular, reusable, and easier to maintain.”



***********आता प्रत्येक pillar सोप्या मराठीत समजून घे.
1. Encapsulation — Data सुरक्षित ठेवणे

public class Job {
    private Long id;
    private String title;
    private String company;

    public String getTitle() {
        return title;
    }

    public void setTitle(String title) {
        this.title = title;
    }
}


JobNest मध्ये: Job class मध्ये job ची माहिती एकत्र ठेवता येते. private fields मुळे data ला थेट access मर्यादित करता येतो.
Interviewer विचारू शकतो: Why do we use private variables?
Answer: To control access to data and protect the object's internal state.

*******2. Abstraction — Implementation details लपवणे
public interface JobRepository
        extends JpaRepository<Job, Long> {
}


JobNest मध्ये: JobRepository वापरून आपण save(), findAll() आणि findById() सारख्या database operations वापरू शकतो. Spring Data JPA त्यांची implementation उपलब्ध करून देते.
Answer in English: “Abstraction allows me to use database operations through an interface without writing their complete implementation myself.”

******3. Inheritance — Existing functionality वापरणे
public interface JobRepository
        extends JpaRepository<Job, Long> {
}


इथे JobRepository हे JpaRepository extend करते.
JobNest मध्ये: Repository ला आधीपासून उपलब्ध असलेल्या database operations चा फायदा मिळतो. स्वतः प्रत्येक CRUD method लिहावी लागत नाही.
Follow-up: Is interface inheritance the same as class inheritance?
No. A class can extend another class, while an interface can extend another interface. Both are forms of inheritance in Java.

*******4. Polymorphism — एक interface, वेगवेगळ्या implementations
उदाहरणार्थ, Spring Data JPA repository interface ची implementation framework runtime ला उपलब्ध करून देते. आपण interface च्या माध्यमातून methods call करतो.
Answer in English: “Polymorphism allows us to work with a common interface while the actual implementation can vary.”
एक महत्त्वाची technical गोष्ट: JpaRepository वापरणे हे स्वतःहून polymorphism चे सर्वात स्पष्ट उदाहरण नाही. Runtime polymorphism दाखवण्यासाठी interface आणि त्याच्या दोन वेगवेगळ्या implementations चे उदाहरण अधिक योग्य ठरते.